  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "21880056",
      "title": "Adding \"Auto Login\"",
      "lectureOrder": 274,
      "videoOrder": 245,
      "sourceHash": "c00ddb5c396933cb8e82a0914f57ff877e515aec64782f1af62596eabf50df1b",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.21,
          "end": 4.81,
          "en": "Now, whilst we implemented Navigation guards,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.81,
          "end": 6.98,
          "en": "I already brought up one problem.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.98,
          "end": 9.76,
          "en": "Whenever we manually enter a URL,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.76,
          "end": 13.13,
          "en": "we lose all our authentication data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.13,
          "end": 15.32,
          "en": "That of course also means that if we leave this page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.32,
          "end": 16.81,
          "en": "and we come back later,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 16.81,
          "end": 19.09,
          "en": "even if we logged in five minutes ago,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 19.09,
          "end": 21.06,
          "en": "we will have to log in again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 21.06,
          "end": 23.78,
          "en": "Because every time this page is reloaded,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 23.78,
          "end": 28.48,
          "en": "we start a new Vue application with a new Vue X store",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 28.48,
          "end": 30.04,
          "en": "and therefore all the data we had",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 30.04,
          "end": 32.85,
          "en": "in the Vue X store before is lost.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 32.85,
          "end": 36.12,
          "en": "That's just how the browser and JavaScript works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 36.12,
          "end": 40.13,
          "en": "But that does not mean that we can't store data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 40.13,
          "end": 42.81,
          "en": "which survives browser reloads.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 42.81,
          "end": 44.82,
          "en": "And therefore, that's the next thing I want to do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 44.82,
          "end": 48.72,
          "en": "I want to ensure that users can stay logged in.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 48.72,
          "end": 50.41,
          "en": "For that, we first of all,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 50.41,
          "end": 53.48,
          "en": "need to go to our auth action",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 53.48,
          "end": 56.3,
          "en": "and restructured a code here a little bit.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 56.3,
          "end": 59.27,
          "en": "We've got the log in and the sign up actions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 59.27,
          "end": 61.05,
          "en": "and the log out actions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 61.05,
          "end": 65.3,
          "en": "I will add a new action auth, which gets a context,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 65.3,
          "end": 69.06,
          "en": "and now I will actually refactor the other two actions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 70.051,
          "end": 72.84,
          "en": "so that we don't have as much code duplication",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 72.84,
          "end": 75.18,
          "en": "because I will now add even more code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 75.18,
          "end": 77.213,
          "en": "that it would be duplicated otherwise.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 78.1,
          "end": 82.15,
          "en": "So I will wrap this code from login and copy it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 82.15,
          "end": 86.043,
          "en": "and add it here in the new auth action,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 87.6,
          "end": 88.93,
          "en": "get rid of console log,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 88.93,
          "end": 90.393,
          "en": "we don't need that anymore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 92.61,
          "end": 95.25999999999999,
          "en": "And here, I now just expect that on the payload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 95.25999999999999,
          "end": 100.25999999999999,
          "en": "which I get here, I also get the mode log in or a sign up.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 100.52000000000001,
          "end": 102.82300000000001,
          "en": "So maybe a mode key on the payload.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 103.87,
          "end": 106.82,
          "en": "And then we've got the URL, which is a variable,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 106.82,
          "end": 111.453,
          "en": "which by default, let's say, is that log in URL here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 113.77000000000001,
          "end": 116.72,
          "en": "But if mode is equal to sign up,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 116.72,
          "end": 120.73,
          "en": "then I want to replace URL",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 120.73,
          "end": 122.66,
          "en": "with the sign up URL,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 122.66,
          "end": 125.333,
          "en": "which we can grab here from the signup action.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 126.46,
          "end": 129.023,
          "en": "Copy it and add it here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 131.1,
          "end": 135.74,
          "en": "And the idea here is that we now simply can use URL here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 135.74,
          "end": 137.61,
          "en": "in the actual fetch function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 137.61,
          "end": 140.32,
          "en": "and reset URL appropriately before",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 141.57999999999998,
          "end": 144.1,
          "en": "and the rest of the code then it's the same anyways.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 144.1,
          "end": 146.863,
          "en": "So here we don't really need to differentiate.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 148.56,
          "end": 151.54,
          "en": "Now, I also want to use async here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 151.54,
          "end": 154.53,
          "en": "so that this still returns a promise",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 154.53,
          "end": 156.51,
          "en": "and we can use the await keyword,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 156.51,
          "end": 158.293,
          "en": "so auth should be async.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 160.49,
          "end": 163,
          "en": "And now we can go to the log in action",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 163.97,
          "end": 167.14,
          "en": "and get rid of all that code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 167.14,
          "end": 169.46,
          "en": "and instead use context dispatch",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 169.46,
          "end": 172.09,
          "en": "to dispatch the auth action",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 172.09,
          "end": 174.57999999999998,
          "en": "here from inside the log in action",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 174.57999999999998,
          "end": 176.29,
          "en": "and pass on an object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 177.3,
          "end": 178.54,
          "en": "where I, first of all,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 178.54,
          "end": 181.97,
          "en": "copy existing payload by using the Spread operator,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 181.97,
          "end": 186.11,
          "en": "hence spreading copying all the key value pairs off payload",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 186.11,
          "end": 188.04,
          "en": "into this new object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 188.04,
          "end": 191,
          "en": "which has passed as a payload to the auth action.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 191,
          "end": 193.68,
          "en": "And then I add mode and set this to log in here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 193.68,
          "end": 196.433,
          "en": "because we need that mode key in the auth action.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 197.55,
          "end": 200.813,
          "en": "And then we can copy that and do the same for signup",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 202.93,
          "end": 204.873,
          "en": "and here set mode to sign up.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 207.38,
          "end": 211.98,
          "en": "Now important, we want to return to result of dispatching",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 211.98,
          "end": 215.1,
          "en": "so that this promise, which is returned by auth,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 215.1,
          "end": 217.86,
          "en": "isn't the end all returned by log in and sign up",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 217.86,
          "end": 221.91,
          "en": "so that our components can still keep track of",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 221.91,
          "end": 224.66,
          "en": "whether we are still waiting for a response,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 224.66,
          "end": 227.76,
          "en": "whether we got an error and so on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 227.76,
          "end": 231.28,
          "en": "With that changed, if I go to log in,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 231.28,
          "end": 233.013,
          "en": "let's quickly test this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 234.29,
          "end": 235.95,
          "en": "This is still looking good.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 235.95,
          "end": 240.95,
          "en": "So looks like we still are able to send these requests.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 242.29,
          "end": 244.51,
          "en": "Yeah, that's looking good.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 244.51,
          "end": 247.463,
          "en": "Signing up with a user that already exists fails.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 248.38,
          "end": 250.11,
          "en": "So now I refactored to this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 250.11,
          "end": 252.2,
          "en": "and I did this for a very good reason",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 252.2,
          "end": 255.36,
          "en": "because now we have to store that data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 255.36,
          "end": 259.6,
          "en": "the token, the local ID, and now, or at least soon,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 259.6,
          "end": 263.43,
          "en": "also the expiration not just in UX,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 263.43,
          "end": 265.84,
          "en": "we do need it there but not just,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 265.84,
          "end": 270.84,
          "en": "but also in some storage that survives page reloads.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 271.75,
          "end": 274.96,
          "en": "And a great example here would be local storage,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 274.96,
          "end": 278.1,
          "en": "which is an API built into the browser.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 278.1,
          "end": 279.78,
          "en": "So it's some browser storage,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 279.78,
          "end": 282.293,
          "en": "which we can access from inside JavaScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 283.6,
          "end": 286.253,
          "en": "For that here, before I commit sets user,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 287.71,
          "end": 291.3,
          "en": "I will access local storage just like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 291.3,
          "end": 293.6,
          "en": "it's available in the browser,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 293.6,
          "end": 296.97,
          "en": "and then call set item to store in new data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 296.97,
          "end": 298.253,
          "en": "in local storage.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 299.8,
          "end": 302.593,
          "en": "And here in the end, I want to store my token,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 303.52,
          "end": 307.853,
          "en": "which I get from response data.id token.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 309.52,
          "end": 313.03,
          "en": "And I also want to store the user ID,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 313.03,
          "end": 316.5,
          "en": "which I get from response data, local ID.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 316.5,
          "end": 318.87,
          "en": "So now we don't just commit it to UX,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 318.87,
          "end": 322.13,
          "en": "but we also store it in the browser storage.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 322.13,
          "end": 325.95,
          "en": "And I'm doing this so that we then also can add an action",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 325.95,
          "end": 329.26,
          "en": "where we check for this data when the app starts",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 329.26,
          "end": 331.24,
          "en": "and when that data is available,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 331.24,
          "end": 334.33,
          "en": "we automatically log the user in.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 334.33,
          "end": 336.49,
          "en": "Because at the moment, if I save that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 336.49,
          "end": 338.27,
          "en": "if we reload this app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 338.27,
          "end": 340.13,
          "en": "if I log in,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 340.13,
          "end": 342.40999999999997,
          "en": "it still works as before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 342.40999999999997,
          "end": 345.3,
          "en": "And when I reload that state is lost.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 345.3,
          "end": 348.37,
          "en": "But now if you go to the Def tools of your browser",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 348.37,
          "end": 351.8,
          "en": "and there to your application in Chrome at least,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 351.8,
          "end": 353.55,
          "en": "you can visit the local storage,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 353.55,
          "end": 354.99,
          "en": "you can view that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 354.99,
          "end": 358.77,
          "en": "and in here you will see a user ID and a token field,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 358.77,
          "end": 360.92,
          "en": "and that's that data which I'd just stored.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 362.09,
          "end": 365.52,
          "en": "And now we can use that to log the user in.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 365.52,
          "end": 368.63,
          "en": "By the way, we can view that data, but it's also our data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 368.63,
          "end": 370.11,
          "en": "So that's no problem.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 370.11,
          "end": 371.913,
          "en": "It belongs to us as a user.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 373.38,
          "end": 375.57,
          "en": "So now we can add a new action",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 376.61,
          "end": 381.61,
          "en": "auto log in or try log in whatever you want to name it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 382.06,
          "end": 383.72,
          "en": "where we do just that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 383.72,
          "end": 385.91,
          "en": "We check whether that data exists",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 385.91,
          "end": 388.933,
          "en": "and if it does, we set a user, if it doesn't, we don't.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 389.98,
          "end": 392.69,
          "en": "So here we also get context.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 392.69,
          "end": 395.65,
          "en": "And then we can access local storage",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 395.65,
          "end": 398.353,
          "en": "and get an item, the token,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 399.23,
          "end": 401.63,
          "en": "stored at in a token constant,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 401.63,
          "end": 403.733,
          "en": "also gets the user ID,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 406.47,
          "end": 411.47,
          "en": "and then check if we got a token and a user ID, let's say,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 411.67,
          "end": 415.313,
          "en": "then I want to context commit,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 416.54,
          "end": 420.9,
          "en": "set user and pass that data on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 420.9,
          "end": 423.7,
          "en": "So here past that payload to set user,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 423.7,
          "end": 426.57,
          "en": "where I set the token to the token we extracted",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 426.57,
          "end": 429.37,
          "en": "from local storage and set the user ID",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 429.37,
          "end": 432.31,
          "en": "to the user ID we extracted from local storage",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 136,
          "start": 433.24,
          "end": 436.9,
          "en": "and set token expiration to null at the moment",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 137,
          "start": 436.9,
          "end": 438.67,
          "en": "because we're not using it yet.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 138,
          "start": 438.67,
          "end": 439.973,
          "en": "That will change soon.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 139,
          "start": 441.26,
          "end": 445,
          "en": "And if we don't have a token or we don't have a user ID,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 140,
          "start": 445,
          "end": 449.47,
          "en": "this will not be committed and we will not set the user.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 141,
          "start": 449.47,
          "end": 452.563,
          "en": "We will not log the user in automatically so to say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 142,
          "start": 453.69,
          "end": 457.39,
          "en": "With that, however, we now need to dispatch this action",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 143,
          "start": 457.39,
          "end": 460.15,
          "en": "whenever our app starts to check",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 144,
          "start": 460.15,
          "end": 462.773,
          "en": "whether we can log the user in automatically.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 145,
          "start": 463.81,
          "end": 467.26,
          "en": "And the best place to do that is the App Vue file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 146,
          "start": 467.26,
          "end": 469.42,
          "en": "because that is our root component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 147,
          "start": 469.42,
          "end": 472.933,
          "en": "This gets created first when the entire app starts up.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 148,
          "start": 474.2,
          "end": 479.08,
          "en": "So here we can add the created lifecycle hook,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 149,
          "start": 479.08,
          "end": 481.85,
          "en": "which has fired when this component is created.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 150,
          "start": 481.85,
          "end": 484.8,
          "en": "And there we can then reach out to our store",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 151,
          "start": 484.8,
          "end": 488.943,
          "en": "and dispatch the try log in action.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 152,
          "start": 490.95,
          "end": 493.43,
          "en": "And with that, if we save this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 153,
          "start": 493.43,
          "end": 495.94,
          "en": "you see if I now reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 154,
          "start": 495.94,
          "end": 498.39300000000003,
          "en": "I actually end up in logged in mode.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 155,
          "start": 500.72,
          "end": 504.84,
          "en": "And I can even reload on requests and we stay on that page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 156,
          "start": 504.84,
          "end": 508.323,
          "en": "So now logging the user in automatically works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 157,
          "start": 509.16,
          "end": 511.56,
          "en": "The only thing we now got to take care of",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 158,
          "start": 511.56,
          "end": 514.41,
          "en": "is that we cleared the data if we log out,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 159,
          "start": 514.41,
          "end": 517.61,
          "en": "because at the moment if I then reload, I'm logged in again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 160,
          "start": 517.61,
          "end": 520.58,
          "en": "because I don't clear the data in local storage.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 161,
          "start": 520.58,
          "end": 524.22,
          "en": "And we also should log the user out automatically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 162,
          "start": 524.22,
          "end": 525.95,
          "en": "when the token expires,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 163,
          "start": 525.95,
          "end": 529.36,
          "en": "because it turns out that the token has a limited lifetime",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 164,
          "start": 529.36,
          "end": 530.853,
          "en": "for security reasons.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
